        "original_id": "4a7722f4-f056-529f-9b61-fd79d4a46a3c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: 11th Academy Awards\n- Films: Grand Illusion, La Grande Illusion, The Great Illusion\n- People: Jean Renoir, Norman Angell\n- Topics: Best Picture, foreign language films, war, European economic interests\n\nFacts:\n- Norman Angell wrote the book \"The Great Illusion,\" which argued that war is futile because all European nations share common economic interests.\n- The film title \"La Grande Illusion\" comes from Norman Angell's book \"The Great Illusion.\"\n- At the 11th Academy Awards, Jean Renoir's \"Grand Illusion\" became the first foreign language film nominated for Best Picture.",
